problem:
Let $V(x)$ be a real-valued function on $\mathbb{R}^{
u}$ with $
u \geq 2$. Suppose that $V$ satisfies the condition $\int_{\mathbb{R}^{
u}} |x|^{-
u + 1} |V(x)|^2 d^{
u}x < \infty$. Prove that the Schrödinger operator $H = -\Delta + V$ has an absolutely continuous spectrum of infinite multiplicity on the interval $[0, \infty)$.
